[{:db/id "q-338378/field-1/e0e0a3ac4fe95f021c8f8aece7092270d36ad30c356733db1e628dc4f0b1d434" :answer/id #uuid "9fcd4b38-1446-5ae3-97ad-552f58e65adb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-338378/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "4e728ba8-2a52-51e7-8d74-28dc61c5396a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-338378/field-1/e0e0a3ac4fe95f021c8f8aece7092270d36ad30c356733db1e628dc4f0b1d434" :answer-field/choices ["q-338378/field-1/e0e0a3ac4fe95f021c8f8aece7092270d36ad30c356733db1e628dc4f0b1d434"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-338378" :question/id #uuid "4a7fff84-7ff5-5fce-a049-e02df71c9444" :question/math-academy-id "q-338378" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964743/assets/601562e6fab230b818a1776e42b700518f803f425dcb7f407d3659e91db0ff33.png)\n\nIf the figure above shows the graph of $f(x),$ then\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{(3f(x)+2)^{2}}{(f(x)-2)^{3}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the power and quotient rules, we can rewrite the given limit as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{(3f(x)+2)^{2}}{(f(x)-2)^{3}} & =\\frac{{({lim}_{x\\to 2}(3f(x)+2))}^{2}}{{({lim}_{x\\to 2}(f(x)-2))}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above is true provided that  ${lim}_{x\\to 2}f(x)$ exists.\n\nWe find from the graph that ${lim}_{x\\to 2}f(x)=1.$ We calculate the limits of the numerator and denominator, separately.\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 2}(3f(x)+2)=3(1)+2=5\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 2}(f(x)-2)=1-2=-1\n$$\n\nSo we have\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{(3f(x)+2)^{2}}{(f(x)-2)^{3}} & =\\frac{25}{-1}=-25.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-338378/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4ad6d0a4-7854-5f87-896c-0c3ba5ef60af"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-338378"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71164/selection/ba9ac19ce07ff19341fc358b4d0726ae551111ebbc034c773af29bf4ee75eb28" :answer/id #uuid "b6fad63a-6769-5a64-bb98-24501b359c74" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12{x}^{6}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71164/selection/83d50d88defd1be5ecc594c3b0c02e891b4f0eaa5df378aa710e353311692af8" :answer/id #uuid "cea061c8-19da-56ce-8d54-dcb7e0787784" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{6}}{4}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71164/selection/85b1b836142bd6879c8eb4f8784322ee7223ed8e8778984348c5e307fdbc3440" :answer/id #uuid "8d8fa5c2-a40d-5a57-be22-aaf96873e790" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5{x}^{6}}{12}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71164/selection/a06590e492b4976b482a5d8e45a9a47e83c106ae67df12380d2162aad9b87130" :answer/id #uuid "55b36c66-5fdf-57f6-86a5-50daa89c7b58" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{6}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71164/selection/fee1903d337982659c277c9117bc72e9c2dc2a12cd8af1248e548d5b10542e7b" :answer/id #uuid "d7af0af2-f981-5a4e-b8c4-3c6596a9d81a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5{x}^{5}}{12}+C" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71164/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1d4d1c21-d2ac-550b-84dd-1ef0c1984175" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71164/selection/83d50d88defd1be5ecc594c3b0c02e891b4f0eaa5df378aa710e353311692af8" :answer-field/choices ["q-71164/selection/ba9ac19ce07ff19341fc358b4d0726ae551111ebbc034c773af29bf4ee75eb28" "q-71164/selection/83d50d88defd1be5ecc594c3b0c02e891b4f0eaa5df378aa710e353311692af8" "q-71164/selection/85b1b836142bd6879c8eb4f8784322ee7223ed8e8778984348c5e307fdbc3440" "q-71164/selection/a06590e492b4976b482a5d8e45a9a47e83c106ae67df12380d2162aad9b87130" "q-71164/selection/fee1903d337982659c277c9117bc72e9c2dc2a12cd8af1248e548d5b10542e7b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71164" :question/id #uuid "820f101a-d00c-5982-8568-97f2eedadddf" :question/math-academy-id "q-71164" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int \\frac{3}{2}{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We can just take the constant factor out of the integral, and then apply the power rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3}{2}{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{3}{2}\\int {x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}(\\frac{{x}^{5+1}}{5+1})+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{6}}{6}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{6}}{4}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-71164/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "add45606-39f6-5a61-9535-867d2950d183"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71164"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122084/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "3ef6b23f-604f-5240-8d10-c59c2a0cb082" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122084/selection/66dedd51c696580d351ab6a45c1c63cb495081ccf219c3c3c62f1d90fbeb5a49" :answer/id #uuid "2b590086-e3b7-5da3-87b0-d6206eb0052e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122084/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "ae07c290-23e0-52d1-95c9-b380b57d031a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122084/selection/303632d9519e4b7e53f9af56aad03bb866b8b5ede58a0b8b2cb848d575460c53" :answer/id #uuid "b31136a5-eaf4-5204-ad5d-af3ae64355bf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122084/selection/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "850e4ac8-2c5a-5363-b704-e476ae06ea6e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/val